./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/method_note_group_averaging.md:1:# Method note — group averaging for hard yaw-invariant conditioning (Route 1, `fa_invariant`)
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/method_note_group_averaging.md:34:`invariant_conditioning()` (src/data/yaw_rotation.py) runs **one full conditioner pass** on the cylindrical-transformed metadata — the pose branch and the RIR audio encoder computed exactly once; the RIR encoder contains BatchNorm, and repeating it |G| times per training step would mutate running statistics (review-caught confound) — then **|G|−1 additional passes of only the two ViT conditioners** (backward-compatible `only_ids` parameter on `MultiConditioner.forward`), rotating depth + ViT-pose keys only (`pose_keys` parameter), and averages just those entries. Cost: ~4× the ViT conditioner compute, ~1× everything else; masks taken from the base pass; the caller's metadata is deep-non-mutated (the eval metric callback reads raw fields afterward).
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/method_note_group_averaging.md:38:Train/eval consistency: the training wrapper (`cond_method: fa_invariant`) and `eval_FLAC.py --cond-method fa_invariant` share the same `invariant_conditioning` and default angles (`DEFAULT_FRAME_ANGLES`); eval composes as rotate-then-symmetrize, which *is* the sanity check; `--cond-autocast bf16` matches fine-tune precision (integrative-review condition C1).
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/method_note_group_averaging.md:57:Matched comparison (fa_invariant + freeze-bn vs vanilla + freeze-bn, identical recipes) yields FA's marginal effect and full-split H1/H2 rotation sweeps on a fine-tuned model despite the lineage blocker; from-scratch `fa_invariant` training is the confound-free route to the absolute Table-1 goals. All infrastructure for both is built, reviewed, and test-pinned.
