./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_15_yaw_aug_claude/yaw_aug_worklog.md:238:- **Analysis — findings the review must focus on (Coder's own list, all substantive rather than cosmetic):** (1) `eval_FLAC.py` records `frame_avg_angles` only under `fa_invariant`, so under vanilla the record reads `null` — the manifest now carries BOTH the effective value and the literal argv flag, each checked against the artifact that witnesses it; (2) the deep gate is a separate module so the 42-cell validator stays torch-free; (3) the arm axis is not an orbit — `EVAL_ORBIT` is now a hard refusal, replaced by `TRAIN_YAW_AUG` asserted against the checkpoint's EMBEDDED `training.yaw_aug`; (4) rotation token moved mid-name per plan §6.7, `parse_eval_name` round-trip verified on all 42; (5) renderers moved out of shell (torch-free validator makes one source of truth possible); (6) production-root lock moved to entry; (7) env namespace `YAW_EVAL_*` with leftovers from the training/exp_14 kits refused outright; (8) exp_11 shared-store thaw/delete cases deliberately de-scoped while a chain is in flight; (9) the "did we touch exp_11/exp_14" check now asks *did WE move anything* and discloses concurrent third-party changes (another session writes there continuously).
