./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/fa_invariant_cond_worklog.md:112:- **Result R0 (zero-shot, frozen ckpt + fa_invariant, K=1, full split):** T60 10.08, C50 1.038, EDT 42.02, R@1 5.38 (baseline: 9.99/1.047/40.11/6.71) — mild OOD degradation as predicted; the fine-tune's job is to close ~0.09 T60 / ~1.9 ms EDT / ~1.3 pp R@1. JSON correctly records cond_method/angles/cond_autocast.
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/fa_invariant_cond_worklog.md:115:- **Command / Validation** — R1 launched per fa_invariant_cond_command.md (updated `0c86c3e`): 10000 optimizer steps, ckpt every 2500, seed 42, commit `0c86c3e`.
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/fa_invariant_cond_worklog.md:130:- **Analysis** — batch parity removed ~35–40% of the R1 regression but the control still fails the primary gate. Combined evidence (R1, R1b, true-online diagnostic): ANY fine-tune of the released checkpoint with this repo's training path degrades energy-decay metrics while preserving AGREE-space retrieval; the effect is not caused by fa_invariant (never enabled in either control), not by EMA-vs-online (≤15%), and only partially by batch noise (~35–40%). Leading remaining suspects for the analysis doc: fresh Adam second-moment transient (optimizer state not released → early steps take outsized parameter-relative moves at any lr), and possible drift between the released-training code and this repo's training path.
