./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/plan_fa_invariant_cond.md:1:# Plan — exp_03_fa_invariant_cond (Route 1: Hard Invariant Conditioning, keep DINOv3)
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/plan_fa_invariant_cond.md:8:Yixun's Route-1 spec (Query 1 in `fa_invariant_cond_yixun_query.md`): symmetrize the conditioner output by frame averaging `(1/|G|) Σ_{g∈G} f(g·x)` over the yaw subgroup G = C₄ = {0°, 90°, 180°, 270°} (Puny et al., ICLR 2022 — `Frame_Avg_pdf.md`), with `f` = the existing DINOv3 + dist_embedder stack unchanged; plus intrinsically invariant **cylindrical pose features** (r, z, Δφ w.r.t. target source) replacing absolute (x, y, z). Both at train and inference. Fine-tune from `FLAC_EMA`, non-destructive recipe, vanilla control gated on exp_01.
./worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_03_fa_invariant_cond_claude/plan_fa_invariant_cond.md:23:- **Scope discipline:** the archived `canon` / plain `frame_avg` eval modes are NOT re-added; one new method name, `fa_invariant`, end to end. Per plan-review: the implementation isolates the two subpaths — invariant pose features vs frame-averaged ViT features — so the method tested is Route 1, not "4× everything".
