worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:69:- **SECONDARY (composite-best checkpoint per arm):** both arms select **step 40,000**; head-to-head FA wins all six. Those two picks are already 5-seed confirmed at BOTH K — K8: FA 8.202±0.017/0.9778±0.0015/38.793±0.074/R@1 5.387±0.075 vs vanilla 8.993±0.011/1.0093±0.0035/40.650±0.101/5.173±0.138; K1: FA 9.543/1.0559/41.754/5.166 vs vanilla 10.287/1.0884/43.437/4.990 → **12 of 14 cells FA, FD the sole exception at both K**.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:83:- **CANDIDATE (not established) explanation for exp_11's reversal:** not "exp_11's small rung amplifies sharing", but simply "**their FA trained with chunk-shared draws; ours (July code) trained with per-angle draws**". Circumstantial support: under the exp_11 recipe their *vanilla* IMPROVED vs ours (T60 8.048 vs 8.993, EDT 37.32 vs 40.62 at 40k) while their *FA* DEGRADED vs ours (EDT 41.50 vs 38.81) — the change that can only touch FA moved only the FA arm.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:95:- **Therefore (a)** our entire B-F arm trained on the legacy **per-angle** loop, so exp_10 did NOT silently change method at the 40k resume boundary — a confound that would have been very hard to detect after the fact, now ruled out by date; **(b)** exp_11's C4L trained with **chunk-shared** draws (micro-8 → all three non-zero angles share one draw). The two arms are NOT the same method at training time; the frame-averaged conditioning differs by ~4% (magnitude corroborated by exp_11's own probe log: eval-bf16 deviation 0, train fp32 and bf16 both ≈3.7–3.9%).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:101:- **Grid:** checkpoints = vanilla P1@40k (matches A4's budget), vanilla anchor@87.5k (our strongest vanilla), FA B-F@40k (per-angle chunk plan, announcement 06). Rotations = 0 deg (have), 90 deg (C4 orbit member), 45 deg (off-orbit control). Seeds 42-46, K=8 first then K=1. Protocol otherwise pinned: EMA, cfg 1.0, steps 1, full unseen split, per-scene mean; each arm under its own cond-method.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:106:- **At 90 deg (C4 orbit member), 5-seed deltas vs unrotated — K=8:** vanilla P1@40k T60 +0.311 / C50 +0.032 / EDT +1.654 / R@1 -0.268; vanilla anchor@87.5k T60 +0.491 / C50 +0.033 / **EDT +5.829** / R@1 -0.470; **C4 FA@40k T60 -0.000 / C50 +0.000 / EDT +0.003 / R@1 -0.006 — flat to three decimals.** K=1 concordant (FA -0.002/+0.000/+0.000/+0.010).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:108:- **Head-to-head under 90-degree rotation, matched budget (K=8):** FA@40k 8.202 / 0.978 / 38.796 / R@1 5.381 vs vanilla P1@40k 9.304 / 1.041 / 42.304 / 4.905 -> **FA wins all four, by wider margins than unrotated.** Against our BEST vanilla (anchor@87.5k, 2.2x the budget): FA still wins T60 (8.202 vs 8.784), C50 (0.978 vs 0.999) and EDT (38.80 vs 41.78), losing only R@1 (5.381 vs 6.489, the anchor's budget advantage).
