worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_yixun_query.md:6:**Assumption/hypothesis:** The exp_07 futility stop was based on mismatched-protocol evals (retracted 2026-08-01: B-F-40k under fa eval ≈ vanilla at matched step). If the trajectory continues normally, fa-from-scratch may reach P1-level (possibly released-level) numbers at the matched 67.5k budget — reopening the from-scratch route the retraction made viable again.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_codex_plan_review.md:3:1. **BLOCKER — R1 is not consistently matched-step and its σ is undefined.** [Plan L18](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/plan_fa_scratch_resume.md:18) compares B-F “endpoint/best” with fixed P1@67.5k, while the candidate may be 55–65k ([L21](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/plan_fa_scratch_resume.md:21)). Make fixed B-F@67.5k vs P1@67.5k the primary; treat best/window statistics separately and compare matched steps. Specify K, evaluation seeds, and P1 mean±SD—an s42 point alone cannot define `σ_c`. Call this matched steps/samples, not matched compute: FA costs ~3.5×.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_codex_plan_review.md:5:2. **BLOCKER — the planned resume pin neither proves B-F lineage nor supports recovery.** [Plan L26](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/plan_fa_scratch_resume.md:26) requires a caller-supplied path but pins only step 40k; inherited checks validate state shape/step, not the checkpoint’s embedded config ([f_arm L169](/home/yixunhu/codespace/FLAC/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_09_fa_finetune_claude/f_arm_launch.sh:169)). Initial launch should require the exact B-F path, embedded `model_config == FLAC_AR_BF.json`, and preferably SHA-256 `5319feb4…2328`. Permit later `EXPECTED_STEP>40000` only for checkpoints inside the exp10 namespace with `MAXSTEPS>EXPECTED_STEP`.
