worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:75:## 2026-08-11T14:36:16-04:00 — A5 PRE-REGISTERED: is exp_11's frame-averaging reversal explained by the chunk-shared RoPE draw?
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:76:- **Mechanism:** `yaw_rotation.py:501` sets `angles_per_chunk = 64 // micro_batch`, so with C4 (3 non-zero angles) exp_11's micro-8 shares ONE draw across all three angles, our micro-32 shares only {90,180}, and the July code (per-angle loop) shared none. FA averages augmentation noise over the orbit; a shared draw correlates that noise so it survives the average.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:80:## 2026-08-11T14:39:05-04:00 — A5 RESULTS: prediction FAILED (no rung dependence) — but chunk-sharing is a real, FA-specific ~4% train-time perturbation
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:82:- **What survives:** the perturbation itself is NOT negligible — **~3–5% relative on the frame-averaged conditioning**, at both rungs — and it is **FA-specific by construction** (a vanilla arm has no orbit, so chunk-sharing cannot touch it).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:83:- **CANDIDATE (not established) explanation for exp_11's reversal:** not "exp_11's small rung amplifies sharing", but simply "**their FA trained with chunk-shared draws; ours (July code) trained with per-angle draws**". Circumstantial support: under the exp_11 recipe their *vanilla* IMPROVED vs ours (T60 8.048 vs 8.993, EDT 37.32 vs 40.62 at 40k) while their *FA* DEGRADED vs ours (EDT 41.50 vs 38.81) — the change that can only touch FA moved only the FA arm.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:84:- **Actionable knob discovered:** `FRAME_AVG_MAX_FWD_SAMPLES` (`src/data/yaw_rotation.py:45`, default 64) sets `angles_per_chunk = 64 // micro_batch`. **Setting it equal to the micro-batch yields one angle per chunk (per-angle draws, the July behaviour); leaving it at 64 gives chunk-shared draws.** FA arms should RECORD the effective chunk plan (cap, micro-batch, orbit size) — different cap values can produce the same partition, so the constant alone does not define the method. Note also that "one draw" is per ViT conditioner *per coordinate* (`conditioners.py:283`).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:85:- **Still open (needs training, ~5 d/arm):** FA @micro-32 with per-angle vs chunk-shared draws to 40k, same recipe — the only decisive test of whether draw-sharing causes the reversal.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:90:  (iv) no local bf16 floor — though exp_11's own probe log corroborates the magnitude (eval-bf16 deviation 0; train fp32 AND bf16 both ≈3.7–3.9%), so ~4% is likely numerically real even if its training relevance is unproven.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:91:- **Status: A5 v1 is WITHDRAWN as evidence.** Its only surviving contribution is the mechanism map (`angles_per_chunk = cap // micro_batch`) and the observation that the code path is structurally FA-only. A v2 with the reviewer's design (fixed B and fixed samples, cap swept at 32/64/96, seeded init, within-schedule dispersion across many seeds, eval-mode + fp32 controls) is running.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:94:- **Dated the code change:** the batched orbit + chunk-shared RoPE draws landed **2026-08-06** (`1479304` batched-orbit invariant_conditioning; `8094d60` disclose the chunk-shared draw). Our FA training ran **7/18–7/23 (0→40k)** and **8/1–8/5 (40k→67.5k)** — both legs finished BEFORE that commit.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:95:- **Therefore (a)** our entire B-F arm trained on the legacy **per-angle** loop, so exp_10 did NOT silently change method at the 40k resume boundary — a confound that would have been very hard to detect after the fact, now ruled out by date; **(b)** exp_11's C4L trained with **chunk-shared** draws (micro-8 → all three non-zero angles share one draw). The two arms are NOT the same method at training time; the frame-averaged conditioning differs by ~4% (magnitude corroborated by exp_11's own probe log: eval-bf16 deviation 0, train fp32 and bf16 both ≈3.7–3.9%).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:97:- **Forward-looking consequence:** retraining FA on the A6000 TODAY would not reproduce our own July arm — current code at micro-32 gives `64//32 = 2` angles per chunk (partial sharing), a third regime. Reproducing July requires `FRAME_AVG_MAX_FWD_SAMPLES = 32`. **Any FA arm must record the effective chunk plan (cap, micro-batch, orbit size); the same config file a month apart is not the same method.**
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:101:- **Grid:** checkpoints = vanilla P1@40k (matches A4's budget), vanilla anchor@87.5k (our strongest vanilla), FA B-F@40k (per-angle chunk plan, announcement 06). Rotations = 0 deg (have), 90 deg (C4 orbit member), 45 deg (off-orbit control). Seeds 42-46, K=8 first then K=1. Protocol otherwise pinned: EMA, cfg 1.0, steps 1, full unseen split, per-scene mean; each arm under its own cond-method.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:105:## 2026-08-12T10:21:06-04:00 — A6 RESULTS (60/60 evals): the rotation head-to-head is DECISIVE, and the 45-degree control validates it
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:106:- **At 90 deg (C4 orbit member), 5-seed deltas vs unrotated — K=8:** vanilla P1@40k T60 +0.311 / C50 +0.032 / EDT +1.654 / R@1 -0.268; vanilla anchor@87.5k T60 +0.491 / C50 +0.033 / **EDT +5.829** / R@1 -0.470; **C4 FA@40k T60 -0.000 / C50 +0.000 / EDT +0.003 / R@1 -0.006 — flat to three decimals.** K=1 concordant (FA -0.002/+0.000/+0.000/+0.010).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:107:- **At 45 deg (off-orbit control) ALL THREE degrade, FA included** (FA K8 T60 +1.438 / EDT +2.108). This is the pre-registered validity check: FA is C4-exact only, so a flat 45-degree cell would have meant broken plumbing, not a better model. The plumbing is sound.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:108:- **Head-to-head under 90-degree rotation, matched budget (K=8):** FA@40k 8.202 / 0.978 / 38.796 / R@1 5.381 vs vanilla P1@40k 9.304 / 1.041 / 42.304 / 4.905 -> **FA wins all four, by wider margins than unrotated.** Against our BEST vanilla (anchor@87.5k, 2.2x the budget): FA still wins T60 (8.202 vs 8.784), C50 (0.978 vs 0.999) and EDT (38.80 vs 41.78), losing only R@1 (5.381 vs 6.489, the anchor's budget advantage).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:109:- **Notable:** the stronger the vanilla model, the MORE it loses under rotation (anchor EDT +5.83 vs P1@40k +1.65) — canonical-orientation quality does not transfer to rotated inputs.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:113:- Verdict `a5v2_codex_code_review.md`: (i) no uncertainty on the increments, and using the same 16 draws for both the mean and the deviations biases the statistic downward; (ii) the fixed-B cap sweep isolates the operational cap SCHEDULE, not pure draw covariance (shapes/RNG consumption still move with the partition); (iii) **the untrained-conditioner limitation remains fatal for explaining exp_11** — the probe describes an initialisation, not either trained arm; (iv) the exact-zero eval cell shows determinism, not a numerical floor for the train-mode increment.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_worklog.md:114:- **Standing:** the monotone ordering is a descriptive pilot observation. It does NOT license "chunk-sharing explains the reversal"; that remains a hypothesis testable only by training (exp_14).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_analysis.md:7:Registered tier **SHORT**: at the fixed 67.5k endpoint, vanilla (P1) beats fa on the decay/spectral metrics while **fa wins all three retrieval metrics at both K** (z 2.9–9.6). The endpoint landed band-worst for fa (outside its own screen band), so the registered verdict is conservative by construction — and the program's matched-step evidence (below) is unchanged by it.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_analysis.md:11:1. **The exp_07 "2×-worse plateau" is definitively an eval-protocol artifact** — under its own protocol, fa's trajectory is band-interleaved with vanilla's: 12/14 displayed cells better at 40k (FD the exception, both K), error metrics tracking vanilla's band through 65k, retrieval leading at some matched points and trailing at others. The REGISTERED endpoint verdict, however, is SHORT — "viable peer" is the exploratory reading, and the registered reading takes precedence wherever they conflict.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_analysis.md:12:2. **Inference-only fa-averaging does not explain fa's matched-step advantage** (decomposition 2×2, all cells 5-seed): applied to vanilla weights it is mixed-to-harmful (retrieval degrades). The pattern is a strong training×evaluation interaction, consistent with a training-side invariance benefit — but with one training seed per arm this is supporting evidence, not clean causal attribution.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_analysis.md:13:3. **Retrieval is fa's most robust edge at the gated points** — all three retrieval metrics lead at both K at the 5-seed endpoint (z 2.9–9.6) and at 40k; at single-seed screen points in between the lead interleaves with deficits (57.5k/60k). 
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_analysis.md:14:4. **Conditioning equivariance is C₄-exact by construction; measured endpoint metrics are near-invariant** (decay/spectral ≤1e-3; retrieval few-hundredths). The 45° control breaks as required. (R3 is contextual — no registered candidate existed.)
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_10_fa_scratch_resume_claude/fa_scratch_resume_analysis.md:18:- The SHORT tier is the pre-registered reading and takes precedence. The endpoint-draw caveat is documented with its own screens; R1b is exploratory and no formal window statistic was computed (single-eval-seed screens). Protocol departures recorded: the S45000 screen was missed (cadence gap → "no qualifier" holds over observed points, full-window coverage incomplete); confirmatory R2/R3 are N/A (no candidate) with endpoint measurements retained as contextual.
